{"$message_type":"diagnostic","message":"cannot move out of `p` because it is borrowed","code":{"code":"E0505","explanation":"A value was moved out while it was still borrowed.\n\nErroneous code example:\n\n```compile_fail,E0505\nstruct Value {}\n\nfn borrow(val: &Value) {}\n\nfn eat(val: Value) {}\n\nfn main() {\n    let x = Value{};\n    let _ref_to_val: &Value = &x;\n    eat(x);\n    borrow(_ref_to_val);\n}\n```\n\nHere, the function `eat` takes ownership of `x`. However,\n`x` cannot be moved because the borrow to `_ref_to_val`\nneeds to last till the function `borrow`.\nTo fix that you can do a few different things:\n\n* Try to avoid moving the variable.\n* Release borrow before move.\n* Implement the `Copy` trait on the type.\n\nExamples:\n\n```\nstruct Value {}\n\nfn borrow(val: &Value) {}\n\nfn eat(val: &Value) {}\n\nfn main() {\n    let x = Value{};\n\n    let ref_to_val: &Value = &x;\n    eat(&x); // pass by reference, if it's possible\n    borrow(ref_to_val);\n}\n```\n\nOr:\n\n```\nstruct Value {}\n\nfn borrow(val: &Value) {}\n\nfn eat(val: Value) {}\n\nfn main() {\n    let x = Value{};\n\n    let ref_to_val: &Value = &x;\n    borrow(ref_to_val);\n    // ref_to_val is no longer used.\n    eat(x);\n}\n```\n\nOr:\n\n```\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)] // implement Copy trait\nstruct Value {}\n\nfn borrow(val: &Value) {}\n\nfn eat(val: Value) {}\n\nfn main() {\n    let x = Value{};\n    let ref_to_val: &Value = &x;\n    eat(x); // it will be copied here.\n    borrow(ref_to_val);\n}\n```\n\nFor more information on Rust's ownership system, take a look at the\n[References & Borrowing][references-and-borrowing] section of the Book.\n\n[references-and-borrowing]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch04-02-references-and-borrowing.html\n"},"level":"error","spans":[{"file_name":"/var/folders/w6/vbftz74j4jzb2t9ry9r724g00000gn/T/mixer-swift-descriptors-uzeruryw/source_drop.rs","byte_start":127,"byte_end":128,"line_start":2,"line_end":2,"column_start":63,"column_end":64,"is_primary":true,"text":[{"text":"fn f(p: ValidatedSwiftReactor) { let bytes = p.source(); drop(p); std::hint::black_box(bytes); }","highlight_start":63,"highlight_end":64}],"label":"move out of `p` occurs here","suggested_replacement":null,"suggestion_applicability":null,"expansion":null},{"file_name":"/var/folders/w6/vbftz74j4jzb2t9ry9r724g00000gn/T/mixer-swift-descriptors-uzeruryw/source_drop.rs","byte_start":110,"byte_end":111,"line_start":2,"line_end":2,"column_start":46,"column_end":47,"is_primary":false,"text":[{"text":"fn f(p: ValidatedSwiftReactor) { let bytes = p.source(); drop(p); std::hint::black_box(bytes); }","highlight_start":46,"highlight_end":47}],"label":"borrow of `p` occurs here","suggested_replacement":null,"suggestion_applicability":null,"expansion":null},{"file_name":"/var/folders/w6/vbftz74j4jzb2t9ry9r724g00000gn/T/mixer-swift-descriptors-uzeruryw/source_drop.rs","byte_start":70,"byte_end":71,"line_start":2,"line_end":2,"column_start":6,"column_end":7,"is_primary":false,"text":[{"text":"fn f(p: ValidatedSwiftReactor) { let bytes = p.source(); drop(p); std::hint::black_box(bytes); }","highlight_start":6,"highlight_end":7}],"label":"binding `p` declared here","suggested_replacement":null,"suggestion_applicability":null,"expansion":null},{"file_name":"/var/folders/w6/vbftz74j4jzb2t9ry9r724g00000gn/T/mixer-swift-descriptors-uzeruryw/source_drop.rs","byte_start":152,"byte_end":157,"line_start":2,"line_end":2,"column_start":88,"column_end":93,"is_primary":false,"text":[{"text":"fn f(p: ValidatedSwiftReactor) { let bytes = p.source(); drop(p); std::hint::black_box(bytes); }","highlight_start":88,"highlight_end":93}],"label":"borrow later used here","suggested_replacement":null,"suggestion_applicability":null,"expansion":null}],"children":[],"rendered":"error[E0505]: cannot move out of `p` because it is borrowed\n --> /var/folders/w6/vbftz74j4jzb2t9ry9r724g00000gn/T/mixer-swift-descriptors-uzeruryw/source_drop.rs:2:63\n  |\n2 | fn f(p: ValidatedSwiftReactor) 